"text": "Sweden built a warship with 64 cannons, and it lost a fight to a breeze. You see, in 1628, Sweden's king ordered a ship to terrify Europe. Before it sailed, 30 sailors ran across the deck. After three runs, it nearly tipped over. So they stopped the test, and sailed anyway. One gust tilted it. A second poured the sea through its open gun ports, 1300 meters out. It was top heavy, and adding weight below would have dropped the gun ports to the waterline. 333 years later, they raised it. 98% intact. A terrible warship. A perfect time capsule.",
